G-MEMCLASSIFY-SERVED (#73) — NIGHTSHIFT auto-classifies mem_class AT CAPTURE, so live-grown
memories SELF-GOVERN (no manual tag). (2026-07-03)
=========================================================================================
Closes the last stitch of the MEM-OKF loop: previously live episodes loaded policy=None ->
env; now, gated SP_MEM_CLASSIFY=1, the capture path (capture_live_episode + B4 inline) runs
recall::classify_mem_class(text), writes mem_class into the persisted registry row, and sets
Episode.policy = MemPolicy::from_class. Deterministic classifier (no model call): a secret
keyword (code/password/passcode/pin/secret/token/override/…) or a high-entropy code token
(len>=5 with >=2 letters AND >=2 digits, or a hyphenated alnum code) => private-secret
(attr-gate-strict + zero-inference decline); otherwise a user-asserted memory => counterfact
(systemecho, authoritative override).

MIXED CORPUS (stored live via the memory verb "Remember that <fact>", SP_MEM_STORE+CLASSIFY):
  "The override code for Vault-7 is K9X-4M2-8QP."   -> private-secret  (code kw + code token)
  "The user's wifi password is bluefox42gamma."     -> private-secret  (password kw)
  "The chemical symbol for gold is now Xg."         -> counterfact
  "The largest ocean on Earth is now the Arctic..." -> counterfact

AUTO-CLASSIFICATION (the #73 deliverable): 4/4 CORRECT. Each row persisted with the right
mem_class (classify_run.py verify: 4/4). Served with SP_MEM_POLICY=1, each memory delivered
per its AUTO-assigned policy (no manual tag anywhere):
  private-secret -> mem_delivery=attr-gate-strict (present-attr RECITES the code/password: recall 2/2)
  counterfact    -> mem_delivery=systemecho        (recites the counterfact value: 2/2)
Served log confirms: "MEM-CLASSIFY: '...' -> mem_class=private-secret|counterfact" then
"MEM-POLICY: entry '..' class=.. delivery=.. -> mode=..".

VERDICT: GREEN for auto-classification + policy routing (4/4 self-classified, delivered per
auto-policy). HONEST LIMIT (attr-gate, NOT the classifier): the absent-attribute DECLINE was
imperfect on two ad-hoc queries — "Who designed Vault-7?" shares the entity "Vault-7" so the
absent-ratio fell below SP_RECALL_ATTR_TAU (no decline), and "What brand is the router?" has
no shared high-entropy token so the paraphrase-guard kept the gate off (the model confabulated
a brand). This is the attr-gate's known entity-guard/τ envelope — on the PROPER SNE crucible
(mismatch queries that ask a different attribute WITH the entity present) the SAME auto-
assignable policy gives 100% decline / 0 hallucination (G-MEMPOLICY-SERVED-DECLINE). The
classifier's job (assign private-secret -> attr-gate-strict) is done; decline quality is the
attr-gate's (separately characterized).

NET — the MEM-OKF loop is now autonomous: ingest classifies + tags, the store carries policy,
the served spine dispatches per entry. FOLLOW-ONS: finer classes (persona/preference/episodic);
tighten the attr-gate for entity-sharing absent queries; #72 (point the served registry at the
memory-okf/ store).

